<title>AUSTRALIA: Electronic commerce major job boon - Australia.</title>
<headline>Electronic commerce major job boon - Australia.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian Communications Minister Richard Alston said booming electronic commerce would be a major source of new jobs, creating up to 300,000 jobs over the next decade.</p>
<p>&quot;It's going to have profound job consequences ... it could mean an extra 300,000 or 400,000 jobs over the next decade,&quot; he told Australian Broadcasting Corp radio from Washington.</p>
<p>Australia has targetted hi-tech sectors, including information technology and computer-based commerce, as a key area to increase employment and tackle the stubbornly high jobless rate.</p>
<p>Official data showed the unemployment rate fell to 8.5 percent in June from 8.8 percent, but largely due to a fall in the participation rate.</p>
<p>-- Canberra bureau 61-6 273-2730</p>
